{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/454159-avoiding-meta-knowledge","id":454159,"title":"Avoiding meta-knowledge","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-23T06:37:25-07:00","id":454159,"title":"Avoiding meta-knowledge","content":"Having just been in a discussion about rolls where your opponents stats are a negative modifier to rolls, it made me wonder if anyone had a good method for using such rules without more-or-less explicitly telling the players what the opponent they're facing's stats are?<br /> <br /> Is that something you as a GM just don't worry about? Or do you have some clever way like not counting the rightmost two or having them roll dice of different colors and picking a few colors not to count?<br /> Stuff like this has also come up for me when the book says &quot;if they fail the roll because of this&quot;, as it'd be hard to say whether the dice they didn't roll would have actually helped.<br /> Anyone have thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T06:43:05-07:00","id":454185,"title":"","content":"Normally I don't worry about my players knowing those sorts of things. If they decide to metagame with that knowledge it doesn't bother me.<br /> <br /> However, sometimes I do like to play up the mystique of something, so if they have to make a roll against something and apply a secret penalty, I do the roll for them behind my hands or a screen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T10:18:46-07:00","id":454548,"title":"","content":"Get in the habit of improvising minor bonuses and penalties other than the ones listed. Being in the actual physical presence of a spirit whose scent you have is probably worth at least a +2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T10:30:45-07:00","id":454562,"title":"","content":"I play almost exclusively online these days, so a DM could easily discount the final few dice of a roll since they're all listed out. Of course, that may make players sad if the last few exploded!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T18:00:12-07:00","id":456400,"title":"","content":"This is a fantastic question, I have often wondered the same thing. Rolling for the player seems to be the best answer, but I'm pretty much too lazy to do that so I just 'fess up the modifier and not worry about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","name":"Mother's Love","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}